---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & Cookie Policy — SFCE Learning"
  description="How SFCE Learning uses essential browser storage and optional Google Analytics cookies, and how to manage your privacy choices."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-text-primary dark:text-dark-text-primary mb-8">Privacy &amp; Cookie Policy</h1>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-text-secondary dark:text-dark-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 2, 2026</p>
      <p>
        This policy covers the SFCE Learning website at sfcelearning.com, including its app information pages.
        The native apps have separate <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}app/privacy-policy/`}>Apple app</a>
        and <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}app/android/privacy-policy/`}>Android app</a> privacy policies.
        You can use the website without an account and without accepting analytics.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
        <p>
          The controller of personal data processed for this website is Krzysztof Kardasz.
          For privacy questions or to exercise your rights, email
          <a href="mailto:contact@sfcelearning.com">contact@sfcelearning.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Essential browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          We store your chosen theme, study progress and privacy choice in your browser's localStorage.
          This storage supports features you request and remembers whether you accepted or rejected analytics;
          it is not used for advertising. Theme and study progress stay on your device until you clear them.
          The privacy record (<code>sfce:cookie-consent</code>) contains your choice, its date, expiry and policy version.
          It is valid for 180 days, after which we ask again. An expired record may remain in browser storage until
          the site is used again or you clear it. These preferences are not sent to Google Analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          This storage is used under the strictly necessary exception in Article 399(3) of Poland's Electronic
          Communications Law. Where personal data is involved in operating and securing the website or remembering
          privacy choices, our legal basis is our legitimate interest in providing these functions
          (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Only after you select “Accept analytics”, we load Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-TZSSJDCPGS)
          to measure visits, use of pages and engagement, and improve the study guide.
          The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and Article 399(1) of Poland's Electronic
          Communications Law). Before consent, or after rejection, we do not load the Google tag or send
          analytics requests, including cookieless measurement requests.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google receives cookie identifiers, page views and interaction information, visit times,
          referring pages, and browser and device information. Your IP address is transmitted as part of
          the connection and may be used to derive an approximate location; Google states that GA4 does not
          log or store individual IP addresses. We do not send your study completion records, name or email
          address to Analytics. Google signals and advertising personalization are disabled by this site's tag;
          we do not use this integration for advertising or decisions with legal or similarly significant effects.
        </p>
        <p>
          Analytics is provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland,
          with processing by Google and its subprocessors. See
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and
          <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12017362">Google's GA4 data collection explanation</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies and retention</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <caption class="text-left mb-3">Analytics cookies are optional and set only after consent.</caption>
            <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose / provider</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Distinguishes browsers for Google Analytics (Google).</td><td>Up to 180 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_ga_TZSSJDCPGS</code></td><td>Maintains session state for Google Analytics (Google).</td><td>Up to 180 days</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          These are first-party cookies. We configure their expiry to 180 days and disable automatic
          renewal on each page load. Browser restrictions may shorten their lifetime. They are removed
          by this website when you withdraw consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          The GA4 property's retention period for user and event data is set to 2 months.
          User-identifier retention can restart on a new visit if the property's reset-on-new-activity
          setting is enabled. Aggregated standard reports are not subject to this same retention period
          and may remain available longer. Cookie lifetime and Google's data retention are separate.
          See <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/7667196">Google's retention documentation</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your choice and withdrawal of consent</h2>
        <p>
          “Reject analytics” is as accessible as “Accept analytics”. Closing the notice or continuing to
          browse does not grant consent. We remember either decision for 180 days in this browser only.
          You can reopen <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer of any page and select “Reject analytics”
          to withdraw consent. This stops further collection, deletes this site's accessible Analytics cookies,
          and reloads the page to unload the tag. It does not erase data already sent to Google or affect the
          lawfulness of processing before withdrawal. Contact us to request erasure where applicable.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also delete cookies and localStorage in your browser. Removing the privacy choice means
          you will be asked again. If your browser cannot save a choice, it applies only to the current page.
          Rejecting analytics does not restrict access to study content or progress tracking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Recipients, hosting and international transfers</h2>
        <p>
          The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub processes connection information, including IP
          addresses, to deliver and secure the site, independently of your analytics choice. See
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>
          for its purposes, retention practices and transfer safeguards. We do not operate a separate server
          that receives your locally stored study progress.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google and GitHub may process data outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States.
          Google describes its reliance on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework for covered transfers to certified
          recipients and on Standard Contractual Clauses where applicable in its
          <a href="https://business.safety.google/adsdatatransfers/">international transfer information</a>.
          Further details and copies of applicable safeguards can be requested from us or the providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your data protection rights</h2>
        <p>
          Subject to the conditions in the GDPR, you may request access to, rectification or erasure of your
          personal data, restriction of processing, and portability of data processed by automated means
          on the basis of consent. You may object to processing based on legitimate interests and withdraw
          consent at any time. We may need information to locate the relevant analytics records, since we
          do not maintain user accounts. You may lodge a complaint with the President of Poland's Personal
          Data Protection Office (<a href="https://uodo.gov.pl/">UODO</a>) or your local supervisory authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>External links and contact</h2>
        <p>
          Linked websites, including Symfony and PHP documentation, have their own privacy practices.
          If you email us, we use your email address and message to answer your request, based on our
          legitimate interest in handling correspondence (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR), or a legal obligation
          where your message concerns a statutory rights request (Article 6(1)(c) GDPR). We keep correspondence
          for the time needed to resolve the matter and meet applicable legal obligations or establish,
          exercise or defend legal claims.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We update the date above when this policy changes and request fresh consent if the purposes
          or scope of analytics materially change. The website's source code is available in our
          <a href="https://github.com/kardasz/sfce">GitHub repository</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  :global(.dark) h2 { color: var(--color-dark-text-primary); }
  section p + p, section div + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  a { text-decoration: underline; }
  th, td { padding: 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); vertical-align: top; }
  :global(.dark) th, :global(.dark) td { border-color: var(--color-dark-border); }
</style>
